## Static verification required before freeze

- Capture the approved P3 `campaign_admission.py` preimage and hashes before editing.
- Inspect the narrow source diff and protected definitions; prove old serialized class definitions and digest expressions are unchanged.
- Audit every `load_typed_state` transitively reachable from both historical public entries. Every call must pass `repair=False`; no `recover_typed_state_index`, state write, artifact write, migration, or repair path may be reachable.
- Audit the new historical call graph for absence of operational services, runtime/request factory/ledger writer construction, provider/API calls, environment reads, nonce generation, and wall/monotonic clock reads.
- Prove policy discovery occurs after the original full round/resource/request/execution/reservation census, role-history authentication, and projection verification.
- Prove legacy absence retains the exact public return and that the summary caller receives no new fields.
- Prove explicit expected-policy absence/mismatch fails and the same authenticated-history helper is called once without public recursion.
- Prove every persisted enrolled request is envelope-checked, every started round is checked at its prior logical prefix, and final report counters come from authenticated ledger/record facts.
- Run only scoped Ruff, in-memory `compile(...)`, AST/source/diff/hash inspection. Do not import modules as a probe, invoke test discovery, read tests, run tests, create synthetic requests/results, or execute a repository reader against fabricated or real campaign evidence during this implementation phase.

Actual immutable archive summaries remain deferred until P1-P4 source review approval and a separately reviewed collector package. At that later gate, run each original archive exactly once, compare the prior 23/27 fields and counts, and prove all 662 archive files plus the 56 evaluator files remain unchanged. Do not attach an admission binding to either old archive.

