## Frozen P3 interface addendum

Interface snapshot inspected read-only: `../admission-p3/review-freeze-01/campaign_admission.py`, SHA-256 `e6b3a9b5362df18d670acd65469e4f4667247743fb93f803ce26041f1cb0dc38`. P3 independent review is still pending; this addendum maps reuse only and is not a P3 spec or quality review.

The freeze adds `_CampaignRoundStateCensusV5` and `_CampaignBoundaryFactsV5`. `_load_campaign_round_state_census_v5(...)` authenticates the policy-selected manifest, original launch/config/owner, contiguous launches/starts, first-round config identity, round config equivalence, and every stored start epoch against the original campaign deadline. P4 should call this once after its original completed-history pipeline and require its returned manifest, launch, config, launch indices, and start indices to equal the already authenticated history aggregate. Its `launches` and `starts` supply the report's configured-round and stored-epoch fields.

`_load_campaign_boundary_facts_v5(...)` authenticates a live settled global frontier and returns evaluated count, attempted count, cumulative attempts/tokens/USD, observed starts, and an optional pre-start round. Reuse its fact meanings, `_role_packages_v5`, `_evaluated_round_indices_v5`, the approved immutable ledger readers, and `campaign_boundary_decision_v5`. Do not invoke the loader retrospectively for each historical round: it requires `next_round_index` to follow every round presently observed, re-runs resource/projection/request/ledger authentication, and intentionally rejects a prior stopping outcome. Once later rounds exist it cannot represent an earlier archive prefix, and using it would duplicate the completed-history authority rather than compose from it.

P4 therefore needs one focused private pure-prefix helper in `campaign_admission.py`, alongside the frozen loader, that accepts the already authenticated P4 rounds/records/packages plus one already authenticated ledger sequence and a prefix end. It should return `_CampaignBoundaryFactsV5` with the same counter semantics and separately expose the evaluated round indices needed by the compliance report. For historical prefix `i`, use only rounds, packages, and terminal receipts with round index `< i`; set attempted rounds and observed starts to `1..i-1`; do not infer a historical pre-start publication or feed later durable state into that prefix. The final completed prefix uses all authenticated rounds. No current time, request object, fake pre-start state, or recursive public authentication is needed.

The P4 aggregate must retain the census-returned start records because `_CampaignBoundaryFactsV5` contains no epochs, and it must retain evaluated indices because that type contains only their count. These are focused report inputs, not reasons to alter either frozen P3 dataclass or its live callers. The completed-history path already rejects unfinished publication, so enrolled completed compliance requires no final `prestart_round_index`; the report must continue to state that cross-file global publication timestamps are unavailable.

Production editing remains unauthorized until P3 passes independent review and the principal explicitly opens P4.
